{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/301274-2nd-ed-abyssals-in-sijian","id":301274,"title":"[2nd Ed] Abyssals in Sijian?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-03T10:42:45-08:00","id":301274,"title":"[2nd Ed] Abyssals in Sijian?","content":"I've got vague memories of it being mentioned off-hand somewhere that there are 10 Abyssal Monstraces that were given to Sijian as a gesture of good faith by one of the death lords. Is this something that actually happened, or is that someone's headcanon I misinterpreted? If it is canon, has anyone ever done anything with these guys? What was yuor experience bringing them to your game, and how did they affect Sijian and the surrounding kingdoms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/768-djehuty3","name":"djehuty3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:20:52-08:00","id":301320,"title":"","content":"I've used Sijan a fair bit in my games (including as character backgrounds), and I've read the bulk of the material on the place. I don't recall any mention of Sijan getting Monstrances. Pretty sure that's someone's headcannon. But hey, if you like it, run with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:32:01-08:00","id":301351,"title":"","content":"From what I read, Sijan and the Death lords are at odds. They play nice with each other and Sijan is trying to keep their neutrality, but the city is preparing for the day where the death lords come a-conquering. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:33:35-08:00","id":301370,"title":"","content":"I think it was Walker in Darkness from the Abyssals book. I think it was one. Personally, I will never use it as an ST that Walker just gives up a Monstrance to Sijan as part of an alliance. Maybe lends the services of an Abyssal. Maybe gives them a Monstrance he still has control over. Sijan with great difficulty Exalts someone, and they think he works for them, but he's working for Walker. Or the alliance is a much, much bigger deal that is hinted at. Maybe another Deathlord secretly runs Sijan? <br /> <br /> If it happened, its a hint about a MUCH bigger story. And not just a Deathlord who wants to secure an alliance with a purely neutral party. Giving a monstrance is like giving someone nukes. It's only done long after an alliance is in place, and for a specific purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:37:31-08:00","id":301373,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't recall Sijan getting any monstrances, much less <i>ten</i> of them. Even if you don't use the 2nd edition numbers that say there are 100 deathknights in all of existence, it's doubtful that any deathlord could afford to give up that many Exaltations as a matter of good faith. Hell, I doubt most deathlords evenhave ten Monstrances <i>in total</i>, considering there's 13 of them sharing the pool of Abyssal Exaltations.<br /> <br /> That being said, Sijan is a fantastic place for an Abyssal game, and the idea that the city might have somehow come into possession of a Monstrance of Celestial Portion or two is an interesting basis for a game, if somewhat implausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:52:01-08:00","id":301387,"title":"","content":"Aren't they somewhat near the Princess' old hangout? I could see after her defeat they collect a few things to keep them safe. Or Walker gives them to Sijan for safekeeping before anyone else. I can see several ways it could happen. I just don't buy that Walker would give up that big of a thing. Or that anyone would, unless it was a trap or a plan (like the Soulsteel Warstrider in Lookshy, or the Royal Warstrider Kejak gave to the Empress).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:53:15-08:00","id":301388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/301274-2nd-ed-abyssals-in-sijian?p=301373#post301373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't recall Sijan getting any monstrances, much less <i>ten</i> of them. Even if you don't use the 2nd edition numbers that say there are 100 deathknights in all of existence, it's doubtful that any deathlord could afford to give up that many Exaltations as a matter of good faith. Hell, I doubt most deathlords evenhave ten Monstrances <i>in total</i>, considering there's 13 of them sharing the pool of Abyssal Exaltations.<br /> <br /> That being said, Sijan is a fantastic place for an Abyssal game, and the idea that the city might have somehow come into possession of a Monstrance of Celestial Portion or two is an interesting basis for a game, if somewhat implausible.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what its worth, there are &quot;spares&quot; that don't correspond to any Abyssal for corrupting the odd Solar. The god of slavery has one, even though its a smelt you into a starmetal bed pan level offense. They are still N/A level artifacts so I imagine the deathlords don't just hand them out like party favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T00:41:43-08:00","id":301923,"title":"","content":"Page 78 of MoEP: Abyssals notes that rumors say that Walker offered a Monstrance to Sijan, maybe even more than one. Just a rumor, but also a fantastic story hook if you want to run a game with some Abyssals who are largely independent of the Deathlords and Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:40:59-08:00","id":302229,"title":"","content":"I kind of got the impression that due to its staus as the acceptable face of shadowlands that Sjian was a rallying point for Liminals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}